abstract: >-
  Reproducibility package for a pre-submission research article testing whether
  biomedical AI benchmark construction changes model selection, hypothesis
  identity, and the evidence concentrated among prioritized hypotheses. The
  package contains frozen cross-domain structural diagnostics, learned-model
  comparisons, stability-controlled DTI and PPI hypothesis-turnover analyses,
  a historical BioGRID later-evidence experiment, an independent ChEMBL 37 DTI
  evidence analysis, negative controls and boundaries, and a leakage-free
  contemporary-model challenge. The package does not claim that structural
  neutralization is universally optimal or that later database additions are
  unbiased biological truth.